MICRO-ENTERPRISE FINANCIAL & CASH FLOW POLICY

1. Working Capital Management:
Micro-enterprises must maintain a minimum cash buffer equivalent to 30 days of operating expenses to mitigate supply chain and revenue volatility.

2. Accounts Receivable:
Invoice payment terms should strictly not exceed 30 days. Automated reminders must be dispatched 7 days prior to the due date.

3. Expense Control:
Discretionary expenditures exceeding 10% of monthly gross revenue require dual authorization from management.
